We’re thrilled to lead General Translation’s Series A.

The best companies today deliberately build their product and services for a global audience. As a result, their products need to be in every language and localized to meet their customers where they’re at.

@generaltxn’s unique approach is full-stack localization. Rather than having designers and engineers rip out translatable text from design and logic, teams can now use General Translation’s developer primitives to integrate directly into their React apps, documentation, and more.

Cursor, Cognition, Ramp, and Clickhouse already use General Translation to scale their products to every language.

@archiemckenzie_ understands both the messiness of language and how to build software that scales, and the result is a product with a laser focus on craft.

By @JenniferHli, @martin_casado, and @JasonSCui

